  "notes": [
   "The selection rule is more complex than the block minimums show. Math requirement: 1 course from Mathematics/Quantitative Reasoning. Depth requirement: 2 courses from EITHER Physical Science OR Biological Science, both from the same department (BIO, CHEM, PHYS, or EOS = AGPS, ENVS, GEOG, GEOL, OCEN, METE). Breadth requirement: 3 more courses, at least 1 Physical Science, at least 1 Biological Science, and 1 more from either. That is 6 courses in total, each at least 3 credits, with a minimum of 18 credits. The Physical Science and Biological Science minimums of 1 reflect only the breadth floor.",
   "The Physical Science list is printed in sub-lists: Astronomy (ASTR); Chemistry (CHEM); Earth & Ocean Science (AGPS, GEOG, GEOL, OCEN, METE); and Physics (PHYS). These are merged here into one Physical Science block, kept in catalog order.",
   "PSCI 211 is printed under Earth & Ocean Science and PSCI 210 under Physics, but PSCI is not named among the depth-requirement departments. ANTH 201, PSYC 202 and AGPS 242 sit in Biological Science, but their department grouping for the depth rule is unclear.",
   "Each list prints 'Units: 0.0' and the sub-headings print '0.0'. These look like system placeholders, so stated was left null.",
   "Total 18.0 is recorded as total_units, consistent with 'a minimum of 18 credits in the area of emphasis'. The 60-credit total is printed as this degree's total, and the page says elective credits may be needed to reach 60.",
   "The emphasis courses also satisfy Cuesta College General Education, and the courses are part of Cal-GETC except MATH 229 and MATH 231. ge_pattern is recorded as Cuesta College General Education, and no GE unit figure is printed.",
